{"nodes": [{"id": "docker_compose_prod_pgp_stack", "label": "Production Compose Stack (pgp)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "1-8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three services on two networks. Deliberately separate from the development file so no production value has a convenient local default to inherit."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_db", "label": "db \u2014 postgres:16-alpine (prod)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "12-35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No ports section at all: the database is reachable only on the compose network, never from the host or the internet \u2014 described as the single most common way a system like this leaks."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_api", "label": "api Service", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "38-120", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built from target 'api', depends_on db with condition service_healthy, joined to both internal and edge networks so Caddy can proxy to it."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_web", "label": "web Service (Caddy Edge)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "123-150", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built from target 'web'. The only published service: 80, 443 and 443/udp for HTTP/3. Certificate volumes survive a rebuild because losing them means re-issuing on every deploy, which Let's Encrypt rate-limits."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_internal_network", "label": "internal Network", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "154-155", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Marked internal:true \u2014 the database and API talk here and it is not routable from outside the host."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_edge_network", "label": "edge Network", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "157", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only Caddy is published; the API joins this network purely so Caddy can proxy to it."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_mandatory_secrets", "label": "Mandatory Secret Interpolation (:?)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "18-23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every production secret uses ${VAR:?message} with no default, so a missing one stops the whole stack rather than silently using a known password. A committed default is a password in git history."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_two_database_urls", "label": "Two Database URLs, Two Roles", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "53-56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DATABASE_URL connects as pgp_app, denied UPDATE and DELETE on Redemption at the database level (R7); DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL connects as pgp_owner. Connecting as the owner would silently remove that guarantee."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_read_only_api", "label": "Read-Only, No-New-Privileges API Container", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "113-117", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing is written to disk at runtime; tmpfs covers /tmp so the image itself stays immutable. security_opt no-new-privileges on both api and web."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_trust_proxy", "label": "TRUST_PROXY Behind Caddy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "71-74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "X-Forwarded-For is trustworthy behind Caddy. Without this every per-IP rate limit shares one bucket and every audited address is the proxy's \u2014 both controls appear present and do nothing."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_internal_cidr", "label": "INTERNAL_CIDR Network Restriction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "132-135", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Space-separated hotel staff/VPN CIDRs allowed to reach both the admin and outlet surfaces and their APIs. Guest Wi-Fi is excluded: network location is defence in depth while authentication remains the primary control."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_jwt_audiences", "label": "Split JWT Audiences (member vs staff)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "67-69", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JWT_ISSUER derived from DOMAIN; JWT_AUDIENCE_MEMBER=pgp-member and JWT_AUDIENCE_STAFF=pgp-staff separate the two surfaces at the audience check."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_identity_code_hmac", "label": "IDENTITY_CODE_HMAC_SECRET", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "62-65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keys the code printed on the back of every physical card. Rotating it invalidates every card at once \u2014 which is also the only recovery a printed credential has, so it must be backed up before a print run."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_sheets_sync_config", "label": "Google Sheets Sync Configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "87-94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Disabled by default; empty values accepted only while disabled, with startup validation requiring all credentials when true. PostgreSQL remains authoritative and Google failures never fail writes."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_outlet_fulfilment_config", "label": "Outlet Fulfilment Configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "96-103", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The guest announces, one outlet confirms. Throttle 60s, expiry 24h, sweep every 900s. OUTLET_NOTIFY_INCLUDE_NOTE is off unless the hotel has agreed the guest's free text may leave the system, because enabling it makes 'we never send names' false \u2014 a guest can type their own into that box."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_resolve_rate_limit", "label": "Counter Lookup Rate Limit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "105-109", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A membership number is sequential and printed on the card, so resolving one is metered (60 per account per hour) no matter who holds the credential. VERIFICATION_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS is 600."}, {"id": "docker_compose_prod_otp_delivery", "label": "SMTP Passcode Delivery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "76-83", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OTP_DELIVERY_CHANNEL defaults to smtp over Gmail on 465. Email is explicitly interim because no SMS provider was provisioned."}], "edges": [{"source": "docker_compose_prod_pgp_stack", "target": "docker_compose_prod_db", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "12", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_pgp_stack", "target": "docker_compose_prod_api", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "38", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_pgp_stack", "target": "docker_compose_prod_web", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "123", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_api", "target": "docker_compose_prod_db", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "43-45", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_web", "target": "docker_compose_prod_api", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "128", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_db", "target": "docker_compose_prod_internal_network", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "30", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_api", "target": "docker_compose_prod_internal_network", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "110", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_api", "target": "docker_compose_prod_edge_network", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "110", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_web", "target": "docker_compose_prod_internal_network", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docker-compose.prod.yml", "source_location": "145", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docker_compose_prod_web", "target": "docker_compose_prod_edge_network", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "conf